{
  "concept": "A change of variables T(u,v) = (x(u,v), y(u,v)) carries a small rectangle S in the uv-plane to a curved region R in the xy-plane, and the Jacobian determinant is the local factor by which that map stretches area.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left panel: uv-plane with horizontal u-axis and vertical v-axis drawn as black arrows, origin at lower-left",
    "Left panel: two vertical blue lines u = u0 and u = u0 + Delta_u extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: two horizontal blue lines v = v0 and v = v0 + Delta_v extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: light-blue filled rectangle S formed by the intersection of those four lines",
    "Left panel: four solid blue corner dots at the intersections",
    "Left panel: labels 'u = u0', 'u = u0 + Delta u' above the vertical lines; 'v = v0', 'v = v0 + Delta v' to the right of the horizontal lines",
    "Left panel: label '(u0, v0)' at the lower-left corner, 'Delta u' under the bottom edge, 'Delta v' beside the right edge, 'S' in the interior",
    "Center: large curved cream/tan arrow with grey outline pointing from left panel to right panel, labeled with the transformation T",
    "Right panel: xy-plane with black arrow axes labeled x and y",
    "Right panel: light-blue filled curved quadrilateral R (distorted parallelogram) bounded by four blue curves",
    "Right panel: the four blue image curves extending past the region corners, labeled 'Image of u = u0', 'Image of u = u0 + Delta u', 'Image of v = v0', 'Image of v = v0 + Delta v'",
    "Right panel: label 'R' inside the shaded region",
    "Optional overlay: tangent vectors (∂x/∂u, ∂y/∂u)Delta_u and (∂x/∂v, ∂y/∂v)Delta_v at the image of (u0,v0), with the approximating parallelogram they span",
    "Optional readout box: area(S) = Delta_u * Delta_v, |J(u0,v0)|, and approximate area(R)"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "transformation",
      "type": "equation_input",
      "teaches": "That the shape of R is entirely determined by the formulas for x(u,v) and y(u,v); changing them restretches and bends the same fixed rectangle differently.",
      "label": "Transformation T(u,v)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "xuv",
          "label": "x(u, v) =",
          "default": "u*cos(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "component"
        },
        {
          "id": "yuv",
          "label": "y(u, v) =",
          "default": "u*sin(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "component"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dragCorner",
      "type": "drag",
      "teaches": "That moving the rectangle to a different (u0, v0) or resizing it changes both the position and the amount of distortion of R — the stretch factor is local, not global.",
      "teaches_note": "drag the corner handles of S in the uv-plane"
    },
    {
      "id": "shrinkRectangle",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "That as Delta_u and Delta_v shrink, the curved region R becomes indistinguishable from the parallelogram spanned by the tangent vectors, so area(R) ≈ |J| Delta_u Delta_v.",
      "label": "Rectangle size (Delta u = Delta v)",
      "range": [0.05, 1.5, 0.05],
      "default": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "showJacobian",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "That the Jacobian determinant is exactly the area of the tangent parallelogram per unit uv-area.",
      "label": "Overlay",
      "options": ["Curved region only", "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian"],
      "default": "Curved region only"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The rectangle S",
      "narration": "In the uv-plane, the four grid lines u = u0, u = u0 + Delta u, v = v0, v = v0 + Delta v cut out a simple rectangle S of area Delta u times Delta v. Everything about it is easy to measure.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 1.0, "showJacobian": "Curved region only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Its image R",
      "narration": "The transformation sends each of those four straight lines to a curve in the xy-plane, and S to the curved quadrilateral R. With x = u cos v, y = u sin v the rectangle becomes a polar 'fan' — straight edges bend.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 1.0, "showJacobian": "Curved region only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Move the rectangle",
      "narration": "Drag the corners of S. The same-sized rectangle produces a much bigger image far from the origin than near it — the stretching depends on where you are.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 1.0, "showJacobian": "Curved region only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Shrink it",
      "narration": "Reduce Delta u and Delta v. The curved edges of R flatten out and R starts to look like a genuine parallelogram.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.2, "showJacobian": "Curved region only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Jacobian appears",
      "narration": "Overlay the tangent vectors at the corner: their parallelogram has area |∂(x,y)/∂(u,v)| Delta u Delta v, which matches area(R) almost exactly. That determinant is the local area-stretch factor.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.2, "showJacobian": "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Change the map",
      "narration": "Type a different transformation, say x = u*u - v*v, y = 2*u*v. The rectangle is unchanged but R — and the Jacobian readout — change completely.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.4, "showJacobian": "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Area doesn't transport for free: a tiny rectangle of area Delta u Delta v lands as a region of area |∂(x,y)/∂(u,v)| Delta u Delta v, and that determinant is exactly the extra factor that must appear inside a transformed double integral.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two side-by-side panels on a white background. Left: black arrow axes labeled u (horizontal) and v (vertical) with origin in the lower-left; a small light-blue (pale cyan) filled rectangle S in the upper-right quadrant, its boundary made of four bold medium-blue lines that overshoot the corners on all sides; solid blue dots at the four corners; serif-italic math labels 'u = u0' and 'u = u0 + Delta u' above the two vertical lines, 'v = v0 + Delta v' and 'v = v0' to the right of the horizontal lines, '(u0, v0)' at the lower-left corner, 'Delta u' centered below the bottom edge, 'Delta v' beside the right edge, and a large italic 'S' inside. Center: a thick curved cream-filled arrow with grey outline sweeping left-to-right and upward, optionally labeled T. Right: identical black arrow axes labeled x and y; a pale-blue filled curved quadrilateral R whose four boundary curves are bold medium-blue and extend past each corner as free curve tails; labels 'Image of u = u0' (upper left), 'Image of u = u0 + Delta u' (top right), 'Image of v = v0 + Delta v' (right), 'Image of v = v0' (lower right), and italic 'R' inside the region. When the Jacobian overlay is on, draw two orange/red arrows from the image of (u0,v0) along the image grid directions and a dashed parallelogram they span, with a small readout panel showing Delta u * Delta v, |J|, and |J| * Delta u * Delta v versus the true area of R. Parse errors in the equation fields should appear inline in red beneath the offending field while the last valid region stays drawn."
}

